== playbook entries (explain-error.sh on each distinct ERROR/WARN/panic line)
  loss-db-connections          2  Postgres refused a new connection (SQLSTATE 53300): in DB mode every lookup that needed one fails RETRYABLY, and a later commit on the partition skips those offsets forever (silent loss of most of a burst, no DLQ)
  loss-retryable-skip          1  the FIRST record of a batch failed retryably, so nothing was committed; if any later batch on that partition commits, the failed offset is skipped forever (no DLQ, no retry)
  (3 distinct line(s) examined; details: explain-error.sh --id <id>)
